Shouldn't this be `get_identifier` to match `OS::has_feature`? The contents of the method are `return get_name().to_lower();`. But then... how is this code any different from this code already in `OS::has_feature`?

	if (p_feature == get_identifier()) {
		return true;
	}

This is the code for `get_name()`:

```
String OS_LinuxBSD::get_name() const {
#ifdef __linux__
	return "Linux";
#elif defined(__FreeBSD__)
	return "FreeBSD";
#elif defined(__NetBSD__)
	return "NetBSD";
#elif defined(__OpenBSD__)
	return "OpenBSD";
#else
	return "BSD";
#endif
}
```

It's different depending on the OS, and gets 'linux' working on Linux again. `get_identifier()` is just this:

```
String OS_LinuxBSD::get_identifier() const {
	return "linuxbsd";
}
```
